th timestamps and idempotency keys; and the UI must distinguish “device offline,” “server unreachable,” and “audience display disconnected” because each has a different recovery path.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_002a496e23ec3bf4016a7e191e16048191bf4e096a26affdce\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_H6vhMQvlcnDGzI0FNev6XRWs|fc_002a496e23ec3bf4016a7e1923d1a08191bbc7e97fa9d6e8c7","name":"todo","arguments":{"op":"done","task":"Research Windows display and offline constraints"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_B4AiqtBVBoEXlWbugSTRxR64|fc_002a496e23ec3bf4016a7e1923d1b081919e9ee74818aed95f","name":"task_send","arguments":{"to":"lead","summary":"Tiered offline model and cache strategy","message":"Offline/PWA lead: do not show a dead generic offline page during a session. Precache the shell, active presentation, current evidence deck, and setup/recovery instructions (cache-first/versioned); treat messages/evidence as network-first with last-known cache; queue presenter-authored notes/commands locally and label them Pending sync. Distinguish Device offline vs Server unreachable vs Audience display disconnected. Show last successful sync time and data freshness on every stale panel. Sources: web.dev service-worker strategies https://web.dev/learn/pwa/serving/ ; web.dev offline fallback https://web.dev/articles/offline-fallback-page ; MDN caching guidance (cache-first UI, network-first recent messages) https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Progressive_web_apps/Guides/Caching ; MDN service workers https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Service_Worker_API/Using_Service_Workers. Do not activate a new app/service-worker version mid-session; defer update to session end to avoid split-version display/console."}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":70461,"output":410,"cacheRead":22016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":54,"totalTokens":92887,"cost":{"input":0.35230500000000003,"outpu